  "goodToKnow": "Der Kleriker is a cleric, a member of the clergy (der Klerus), used for Christian and also Muslim religious leaders in news. The everyday German word is der Geistliche (declined like an adjective) or der Pfarrer. Klerikal means clerical, of the clergy, not office work (that's Büro-). Antiklerikal movements opposed church influence in the 19th-century Kulturkampf. The plural is the same."
